rd68021_ucode_rom: a microcode store Quartus builds in block RAM

On a MAX 10 10M50 (the Arrow DECA running the Sun-3/60 replica) Quartus
built the 103 x 4096 store from ~4,700 logic elements, and the path from the
bus unit's falling-edge early_q into rom_q, which has half a clock period,
crossed that whole cone: 30.9 ns to 36.3 ns depending on placement, which
failed timing at 16.667 MHz (-0.93 ns) and at 15.625 MHz (-4.27 ns).

Two reasons, both Quartus's:
 * it reads romstyle, not rom_style (Warning 10335);
 * it infers no ROM from a case whose 12-bit index has fewer than half its
   entries labelled -- 1906 of 4096 here -- whatever the attribute says.
   Tried alone: romstyle, ramstyle, no reset gating on the address, a plain
   always block and a 36-bit slice all stay in logic; an 11-bit index gives
   0 LE and 210,944 bits (26 M9K).

So the case takes the low eleven bits and bit 11, registered with it,
selects the entry `default' gives every address from 1906 up: the same
function, and 115 LE + 26 M9K.  Vivado reads it the same way.

Against RD68021 33d9289.  Better fixed in the generator; to drop then.

--- a/rtl/gen/rd68021_ucode_rom.sv
+++ b/rtl/gen/rd68021_ucode_rom.sv
@@ -45,12 +45,22 @@
   // with no message. The attribute is on a register DECLARATION, which is where
   // both tools look for it -- on the always block Quartus ignores it with
   // Warning 10335 -- and Quartus picks the block type for the family itself.
-  (* rom_style = "block" *)
+  //
+  // Quartus reads romstyle, not rom_style -- and it infers no ROM at all from
+  // a case whose 12-bit index has fewer than half its entries labelled, which
+  // this one (1906 of 4096) has.  So the case is indexed by the low eleven
+  // bits, and bit 11, registered alongside, selects the illegal entry that
+  // `default' gives every address from 1906 up.  Same function; on a MAX 10
+  // 26 M9K and ~115 LE instead of ~4,700 LE.
+  (* rom_style = "block", romstyle = "M9K" *)
   logic [102:0] rom_q;
-  assign uw = rom_q;
+  logic         hi_q;
+  wire  [10:0]  a_lo = a[10:0];
+  always_ff @(posedge clk) hi_q <= a[11];
+  assign uw = hi_q ? 103'h00000000001000000010127400 : rom_q;
 
   always_ff @(posedge clk) begin
-      case (a)
+      case (a_lo)
         12'd0    : rom_q <= 103'h00000000001100002A00400400;   // the initial interrupt stack pointer, from $0 / ... into the active stack pointer
         12'd1    : rom_q <= 103'h40000000001000000201400800;   // the initial program counter, from $4
         12'd2    : rom_q <= 103'h00000000C01000002810000C00;   // ... and start fetching there
